(373850, 30617, 3306, '<td valign="top">Nice try, but out of focus.</td>', 'Nice try, but out of focus.', '2003-08-01 19:00:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(373869, 31021, 7743, '<td valign="top">The amount of DOF you used here is appropropriate but  a slight shift backwards may work better to get less of the foreground and more of the bug in focus.<br/> <br/>Good contrast with the pruple flowers and green foliage.</td>', 'The amount of DOF you used here is appropropriate but  a slight shift backwards may work better to get less of the foreground and more of the bug in focus. Good contrast with the pruple flowers and green foliage.', '2003-08-01 19:13:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(373873, 30456, 7743, '<td valign="top">Your title says it all.  It''s hard to tell his front end from his back end.  Though it seems a little dark on the right the lighting on the left is good.  A reflector or a flashlight may help in these situations to balance the lighting..</td>', 'Your title says it all.  It''s hard to tell his front end from his back end.  Though it seems a little dark on the right the lighting on the left is good.  A reflector or a flashlight may help in these situations to balance the lighting..', '2003-08-01 19:17:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(373877, 30899, 7743, '<td valign="top">You''ve captured lots of detail in this closeup though maybe the image could benefit from a little more DOF.  Lighting is good, maybe just a tad too bright on the right.  The bright green background is a bit distracting as well.</td>', 'You''ve captured lots of detail in this closeup though maybe the image could benefit from a little more DOF.  Lighting is good, maybe just a tad too bright on the right.  The bright green background is a bit distracting as well.', '2003-08-01 19:20:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(373878, 30741, 7743, '<td valign="top">It''s always hard to get a balanced image when part of the picture is in bright sunshine and the other part is in shade.  You''ve done a good job to try and limit the amount of bright area in your photo though your foreground still appears to be a bit underexposed.  To try and solve this without blowing out the sky you could try using a graduated ND filter to tone down the background and allow you to expose more for the foreground.  This would probably work since the transition between bright and shade is in a fairly straight line.</td>', 'It''s always hard to get a balanced image when part of the picture is in bright sunshine and the other part is in shade.  You''ve done a good job to try and limit the amount of bright area in your photo though your foreground still appears to be a bit underexposed.  To try and solve this without blowing out the sky you could try using a graduated ND filter to tone down the background and allow you to expose more for the foreground.  This would probably work since the transition between bright and shade is in a fairly straight line.', '2003-08-01 19:30:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(373881, 31127, 7743, '<td valign="top">Composition and exposure are good.   You have used DOF to your advantage though your subject could possibly benefit from sharper focus.</td>', 'Composition and exposure are good.   You have used DOF to your advantage though your subject could possibly benefit from sharper focus.', '2003-08-01 19:35:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(373882, 31224, 7743, '<td valign="top">Your image seems to be well exposed though the focal point of the image leads the eye off the edge at the top.  To keep the viewer inside the boundaries of the frame you might of tried to keep the leaves in the lower left in focus rather than the ones on top.</td>', 'Your image seems to be well exposed though the focal point of the image leads the eye off the edge at the top.  To keep the viewer inside the boundaries of the frame you might of tried to keep the leaves in the lower left in focus rather than the ones on top.', '2003-08-01 19:39:44.000000', NULL, 1),
