(376153, 31075, 4258, '<td valign="top">Too small</td>', 'Too small', '2003-08-04 10:06:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(376154, 31028, 917, '<td valign="top">A bit bright, try shading the area. Also, this is not normal behaviour for bees (or is it a wasp?, its got a hairy thorax and a smooth abdomen. My guess is a cuckoo bee), I''d prefer to see it doing something more ''exiting'' than playing dead.  <br/>Photographically, youve used rule of thirds, but the body is facing out of frame, rather than into the space created by rule of thirds. Try putting the bee in on the right, which would also move the background out and more foreground leaf in.</td>', 'A bit bright, try shading the area. Also, this is not normal behaviour for bees (or is it a wasp?, its got a hairy thorax and a smooth abdomen. My guess is a cuckoo bee), I''d prefer to see it doing something more ''exiting'' than playing dead.  Photographically, youve used rule of thirds, but the body is facing out of frame, rather than into the space created by rule of thirds. Try putting the bee in on the right, which would also move the background out and more foreground leaf in.', '2003-08-04 10:07:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(376155, 30869, 917, '<td valign="top">I think is better with a bit more off the top.</td>', 'I think is better with a bit more off the top.', '2003-08-04 10:08:40.000000', NULL, 1),
