(377418, 30890, 2337, '<td valign="top">You''re not suppose to have a flower as the subject of your shot :) Just kidding :)<br/> <br/>Seriously, I am bothered by the angle... I think you would have had a better shot if the shadows were straighter and maybe if possible, if the bottom could have been closer to the feet.... I think portrait layout would have suited this best.<br/> <br/>But that''s just me :)</td>', 'You''re not suppose to have a flower as the subject of your shot :) Just kidding :) Seriously, I am bothered by the angle... I think you would have had a better shot if the shadows were straighter and maybe if possible, if the bottom could have been closer to the feet.... I think portrait layout would have suited this best. But that''s just me :)', '2003-08-05 16:36:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(377421, 30593, 3575, '<td valign="top">Love it! How close did you have to get? I''ll make a point to come back and get the story. Very nice. 10</td>', 'Love it! How close did you have to get? I''ll make a point to come back and get the story. Very nice. 10', '2003-08-05 16:38:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(377422, 30585, 5603, '<td valign="top">I would love this photo if it had a different subject.  The worm seems very stressed out like it hasn''t eaten in some time and it pains me to see such sadness in this world.  Feed it next time then photograph it please.</td>', 'I would love this photo if it had a different subject.  The worm seems very stressed out like it hasn''t eaten in some time and it pains me to see such sadness in this world.  Feed it next time then photograph it please.', '2003-08-05 16:38:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(377425, 30995, 2337, '<td valign="top">Great use of repetition! One of the best shots I''ve seen this challenge... Congratulations</td>', 'Great use of repetition! One of the best shots I''ve seen this challenge... Congratulations', '2003-08-05 16:39:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(377430, 31075, 2337, '<td valign="top">I feel this shot was seriously hurt by the size... You are allowed 640 pixels on one side and up to 150k file size.  So your shot was about one third the size it could have been.... It''s very hard to judge how good the shot itself might be.</td>', 'I feel this shot was seriously hurt by the size... You are allowed 640 pixels on one side and up to 150k file size.  So your shot was about one third the size it could have been.... It''s very hard to judge how good the shot itself might be.', '2003-08-05 16:42:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(377434, 31130, 3575, '<td valign="top">Nice job getting the exposure right. You probably used a polarizer?</td>', 'Nice job getting the exposure right. You probably used a polarizer?', '2003-08-05 16:48:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(377439, 30834, 3575, '<td valign="top">OK, I LOVE this shot. I like that you took it from the ant''s perspective, the DOF is just perfect. The dry grass and just a little green is very interesting and helps the little ant stand out. This is one of my favorites this time. Nice job 10</td>', 'OK, I LOVE this shot. I like that you took it from the ant''s perspective, the DOF is just perfect. The dry grass and just a little green is very interesting and helps the little ant stand out. This is one of my favorites this time. Nice job 10', '2003-08-05 16:51:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(377444, 30703, 2337, '<td valign="top">Interesting concept for the challenge... However, I feel your execution missed on a couple of points... <br/> <br/>The table to the right and below the Bible adds nothing... Crop it out :)  <br/> <br/>If you could have found a better light source that would give an even illumination it would have been a big help too... To see what I mean, look at Chapter 2, Verse 23 and compare the readability to Chapter 3, Verse 3...  The light on 3:3 is much harsher and makes it more difficult to see...  To be "a light unto the world", you will need to master lighting a little better :)<br/> <br/>The focus on parts of the apple are off...  I feel this could have been a MUCH better shot if it had been much closer in and only had the bitten part of the apple...<br/> <br/>Last, but certainly not least, the Bible should (in my opinion) be straight... It is severely slanted here...<br/> <br/>Great concept though... Nice interpretation of the challenge.</td>', 'Interesting concept for the challenge... However, I feel your execution missed on a couple of points...  The table to the right and below the Bible adds nothing... Crop it out :)   If you could have found a better light source that would give an even illumination it would have been a big help too... To see what I mean, look at Chapter 2, Verse 23 and compare the readability to Chapter 3, Verse 3...  The light on 3:3 is much harsher and makes it more difficult to see...  To be "a light unto the world", you will need to master lighting a little better :) The focus on parts of the apple are off...  I feel this could have been a MUCH better shot if it had been much closer in and only had the bitten part of the apple... Last, but certainly not least, the Bible should (in my opinion) be straight... It is severely slanted here... Great concept though... Nice interpretation of the challenge.', '2003-08-05 16:52:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(377449, 30891, 3575, '<td valign="top">Beautiful scene and lovely perspective of the garden. Only thing I don''t like is the washed out sky. Because of the shadows, I know that the day was sunny. If you can use a polarizer with your camera, this would be a great reason to use it.</td>', 'Beautiful scene and lovely perspective of the garden. Only thing I don''t like is the washed out sky. Because of the shadows, I know that the day was sunny. If you can use a polarizer with your camera, this would be a great reason to use it.', '2003-08-05 16:56:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(377450, 30270, 2337, '<td valign="top">Nice concept... You may want to look for better lighting sources though... Also, the table doesn''t add to the shot and should be cropped out :)</td>', 'Nice concept... You may want to look for better lighting sources though... Also, the table doesn''t add to the shot and should be cropped out :)', '2003-08-05 16:57:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(377457, 30283, 10869, '<td valign="top">that flower is one of the main component of your picture =&gt; it doesn''t really meet the challenge then.</td>', 'that flower is one of the main component of your picture => it doesn''t really meet the challenge then.', '2003-08-05 17:09:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(377488, 30830, 280, '<td valign="top">I like the idea, although the highlights on the brim of his hat and the back of his leg are too bright. Would have been tempted to title it Medic! myself, Good luck.   Tom</td>', 'I like the idea, although the highlights on the brim of his hat and the back of his leg are too bright. Would have been tempted to title it Medic! myself, Good luck.   Tom', '2003-08-05 18:23:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(377495, 30582, 10921, '<td valign="top">Pretty cool. Congrats.</td>', 'Pretty cool. Congrats.', '2003-08-05 18:27:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(377512, 31195, 6525, '<td valign="top">Great job on a terrific picture. At first I thought it was a little 2 busy and no central focal point, was it the the main water coming up, the bird sitting on the ledge or was it the drops of water? But after much thought I have to tell you that this is my favorite picture and the more that I look at it the more that I like it.</td>', 'Great job on a terrific picture. At first I thought it was a little 2 busy and no central focal point, was it the the main water coming up, the bird sitting on the ledge or was it the drops of water? But after much thought I have to tell you that this is my favorite picture and the more that I look at it the more that I like it.', '2003-08-05 18:43:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(377513, 30959, 509, '<td valign="top">A little overexposed.  If your camera doesn''t have the option of manually setting the exposure, I would have aimed the camera at a subject slightly brighter than the child, half pressed the shutter, and then recompose this subject before fully pressing the shutter.  It might also give a little more color to the shot.</td>', 'A little overexposed.  If your camera doesn''t have the option of manually setting the exposure, I would have aimed the camera at a subject slightly brighter than the child, half pressed the shutter, and then recompose this subject before fully pressing the shutter.  It might also give a little more color to the shot.', '2003-08-05 18:47:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(377514, 30879, 509, '<td valign="top">The reflection of the light really sells this shot.  I like the contrasts between the lighter and darker elements as well.  I think the image would stand well alone without the border though (yeah, it''s small, but i''m stretching for some sort of criticim = )  Nice work.  -10- Mav</td>', 'The reflection of the light really sells this shot.  I like the contrasts between the lighter and darker elements as well.  I think the image would stand well alone without the border though (yeah, it''s small, but i''m stretching for some sort of criticim = )  Nice work.  -10- Mav', '2003-08-05 18:50:00.000000', NULL, 1),
