(377965, 31033, 2586, '<td valign="top">Having looked thus far, i would say this is one of the best shots in the challenge. Very beautiful and original. You really hurt yourself badly by submitting such a small size pic.</td>', 'Having looked thus far, i would say this is one of the best shots in the challenge. Very beautiful and original. You really hurt yourself badly by submitting such a small size pic.', '2003-08-06 02:02:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(377969, 30751, 2011, '<td valign="top">Beautiful, beautiful shot Mieka!  Keep it up.</td>', 'Beautiful, beautiful shot Mieka!  Keep it up.', '2003-08-06 02:05:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(377979, 31189, 2586, '<td valign="top">I didn''t vote and only browsed through the thumbs (even now i have only bothered to look at 2-3 pics :) and figured this fountain was yours. What''s bothersome is the green stuff on the right (line, guy, and wall). Even though the fountain is beautiful, those vivid colors are very close to the edge of an otherwise fairly dark picture and pull the eye out of it. Without the greenish stuff on the right, this would be a good picture.</td>', 'I didn''t vote and only browsed through the thumbs (even now i have only bothered to look at 2-3 pics :) and figured this fountain was yours. What''s bothersome is the green stuff on the right (line, guy, and wall). Even though the fountain is beautiful, those vivid colors are very close to the edge of an otherwise fairly dark picture and pull the eye out of it. Without the greenish stuff on the right, this would be a good picture.', '2003-08-06 02:11:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(377991, 30356, 6388, '<td valign="top">This is fabulous helene.  I laughed out loud.  Great job at getting the sepia tones...better than most. great perspective, great crop.  Little bit tongue in cheek, which I like, but likely accounted for some people not taking it as seriously as they should have.  Again - something completely new for you.  Again, I''m impressed.<br/> <br/>Pedro</td>', 'This is fabulous helene.  I laughed out loud.  Great job at getting the sepia tones...better than most. great perspective, great crop.  Little bit tongue in cheek, which I like, but likely accounted for some people not taking it as seriously as they should have.  Again - something completely new for you.  Again, I''m impressed. Pedro', '2003-08-06 02:18:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(377992, 31244, 8682, '<td valign="top">Congrats Indigo! It´s a brilliant shot, it was a shame that you didn´t get a ribbon... Green ribbon!<br/>God job.<br/>Take care &amp; Have fun</td>', 'Congrats Indigo! It´s a brilliant shot, it was a shame that you didn´t get a ribbon... Green ribbon!God job.Take care & Have fun', '2003-08-06 02:18:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(378028, 30597, 6525, '<td valign="top">Photoshop? Yes indeed and I think it is legal so long as you apply it to the entire image. Anyway, I learned it from one of the tutorials here in DP Challenge a photograph called "Rest" by fellow photographer Miller</td>', 'Photoshop? Yes indeed and I think it is legal so long as you apply it to the entire image. Anyway, I learned it from one of the tutorials here in DP Challenge a photograph called "Rest" by fellow photographer Miller', '2003-08-06 02:37:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(378040, 31219, 6525, '<td valign="top">I am sorry that I was unable to vote for your image because if I had I would have given it a 10 rating! In this challenge this is the first non-bug picture to score this high and IMHO you hit the mark better than any one else as far as being on target with the theme and by far the most creative. Great job!</td>', 'I am sorry that I was unable to vote for your image because if I had I would have given it a 10 rating! In this challenge this is the first non-bug picture to score this high and IMHO you hit the mark better than any one else as far as being on target with the theme and by far the most creative. Great job!', '2003-08-06 02:49:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(378046, 31186, 9073, '<td valign="top">I don''t know why I missed this shot during the challenge. And I''m surprised that it scored so lowly. It''s a wonderfully intelligent shot. I really like the way you''ve shown the ''wings'' of the flower in contrast to the ''leaves'' of the butterfly. The branch creates a very strong and effective line dividing the two. Good balance and good contrast. I would have given you a ten.</td>', 'I don''t know why I missed this shot during the challenge. And I''m surprised that it scored so lowly. It''s a wonderfully intelligent shot. I really like the way you''ve shown the ''wings'' of the flower in contrast to the ''leaves'' of the butterfly. The branch creates a very strong and effective line dividing the two. Good balance and good contrast. I would have given you a ten.', '2003-08-06 02:52:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(378058, 30679, 1143, '<td valign="top">I liked this shot a lot and gave it a 7 (which is high for me), but I think it has some issues. All of the background stalks are really distracting. It might work better as a close-up of the individual ear. I like the b&amp;w choice a lot. Maybe you could try one not totally desat with the kernels still yellow.. something to help it stand out more.  I like that the front plant gives the picture some depth, but it''s a little distracting that it''s so large and blurry. Fits the topic well though.</td>', 'I liked this shot a lot and gave it a 7 (which is high for me), but I think it has some issues. All of the background stalks are really distracting. It might work better as a close-up of the individual ear. I like the b&w choice a lot. Maybe you could try one not totally desat with the kernels still yellow.. something to help it stand out more.  I like that the front plant gives the picture some depth, but it''s a little distracting that it''s so large and blurry. Fits the topic well though.', '2003-08-06 02:57:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(378068, 30431, 5892, '<td valign="top">You know what I really like about this photo? Is that you didn''t push the blue until it looked unnatural. These berries look real to me... wholesome. The whole idea of it is refreshing, as we usually see the ''perfect'' colors here on DPC. A highly underrated shot IMO! Great job. Thanks for the breath of fresh air.</td>', 'You know what I really like about this photo? Is that you didn''t push the blue until it looked unnatural. These berries look real to me... wholesome. The whole idea of it is refreshing, as we usually see the ''perfect'' colors here on DPC. A highly underrated shot IMO! Great job. Thanks for the breath of fresh air.', '2003-08-06 03:02:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(378069, 30576, 1143, '<td valign="top">Very strong shot. It stood out from the rest when I went through the thumbnails. Very shallow dof, but it works nicely. Is this a custom quadtone? I really think this would''ve done better in a different challenge which is unfortunate. It''s definitely better than a most of the pictures above it. Giving it the title "memorial garden" would''ve probably helped.<br/>Nice title too   ;)  I uploaded my snake pic two minutes before the deadline so I just put the first thing that came into my mind. Maybe I should just start leaving them blank because I rarely come up with anything good.</td>', 'Very strong shot. It stood out from the rest when I went through the thumbnails. Very shallow dof, but it works nicely. Is this a custom quadtone? I really think this would''ve done better in a different challenge which is unfortunate. It''s definitely better than a most of the pictures above it. Giving it the title "memorial garden" would''ve probably helped.Nice title too   ;)  I uploaded my snake pic two minutes before the deadline so I just put the first thing that came into my mind. Maybe I should just start leaving them blank because I rarely come up with anything good.', '2003-08-06 03:05:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(378075, 30969, 9027, '<td valign="top">hi pups. this one was kinda scary because of all the fingers. O_o but i thought it cute.</td>', 'hi pups. this one was kinda scary because of all the fingers. O_o but i thought it cute.', '2003-08-06 03:09:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(378082, 31144, 5313, '<td valign="top">That''s a fantastic shot.  I can''t get over the colouring on the dragonfly!  Just amazing!<br/> <br/></td>', 'That''s a fantastic shot.  I can''t get over the colouring on the dragonfly!  Just amazing! ', '2003-08-06 03:15:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(378085, 31244, 1143, '<td valign="top">We''ve found several snakes under wood in the yard recently. This was the smallest I''d ever seen though. I kept it in a little glass aquarium for a day so that the kids could see it.<br/>I had a really hard time coming up with a way to shoot him. I have some shots of the kids holding him, and he looks tiny even in their hands. It''s amazing how fast he is ... I had to drape a laundry basket in black fabric and place it under him. I don''t need a baby snake loose in the bedroom!<br/>I have other shots with better composition, but this was the only one where I caught his tongue out. He came out to the edge of the front flower and was reaching toward my camera as if he wanted to say hello.<br/> <br/>Macro lens +4, bounced flash, f 2.5, 1/160, ISO 200 (thus the noise in the background), levels adjusted slightly</td>', 'We''ve found several snakes under wood in the yard recently. This was the smallest I''d ever seen though. I kept it in a little glass aquarium for a day so that the kids could see it.I had a really hard time coming up with a way to shoot him. I have some shots of the kids holding him, and he looks tiny even in their hands. It''s amazing how fast he is ... I had to drape a laundry basket in black fabric and place it under him. I don''t need a baby snake loose in the bedroom!I have other shots with better composition, but this was the only one where I caught his tongue out. He came out to the edge of the front flower and was reaching toward my camera as if he wanted to say hello. Macro lens +4, bounced flash, f 2.5, 1/160, ISO 200 (thus the noise in the background), levels adjusted slightly', '2003-08-06 03:18:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(378088, 30463, 5313, '<td valign="top">Oh, Ursula!  That''s amazing!  I love to see the water droplets like that!  Great job!</td>', 'Oh, Ursula!  That''s amazing!  I love to see the water droplets like that!  Great job!', '2003-08-06 03:20:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(378093, 30751, 5313, '<td valign="top">That''s gorgeous, Mieka!  I love that wheel and all the cacti.<br/> <br/>Great shot!<br/> <br/></td>', 'That''s gorgeous, Mieka!  I love that wheel and all the cacti. Great shot! ', '2003-08-06 03:22:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(378098, 31144, 3554, '<td valign="top">My favorite dragonfly shot. Congrats!</td>', 'My favorite dragonfly shot. Congrats!', '2003-08-06 03:23:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(378103, 30929, 3554, '<td valign="top">I was sure this was a ribbon, but some tough competition.  Again, great shot.</td>', 'I was sure this was a ribbon, but some tough competition.  Again, great shot.', '2003-08-06 03:26:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(378116, 31044, 3554, '<td valign="top">I was surprised this wasn''t a bit higher. I liked that the wings were cropped but I think I''m a minority.  :)</td>', 'I was surprised this wasn''t a bit higher. I liked that the wings were cropped but I think I''m a minority.  :)', '2003-08-06 03:32:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(378134, 31144, 5728, '<td valign="top">Woohoo way to go, excellent win! Have you corked the champagne yet?<br/></td>', 'Woohoo way to go, excellent win! Have you corked the champagne yet?', '2003-08-06 03:56:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(378136, 31219, 8298, '<td valign="top">very nice ella</td>', 'very nice ella', '2003-08-06 03:56:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(378137, 30593, 5728, '<td valign="top">Way to go Buzz, you finally got your ribbon, choice!<br/></td>', 'Way to go Buzz, you finally got your ribbon, choice!', '2003-08-06 03:57:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(378144, 30964, 9661, '<td valign="top">So despite another commentor saying essentially the same thing as me it''s me who is at fault for not seeing the challenge? Thanks for the PM and I quote..<br/> <br/>ooooh, I''m sorry.  I realise now I should have done a butterfly sitting on gnome.  Live and learn.<br/> <br/>IMHO to become a better photographer you need to accept criticism better, it''s not personal, I don''t know you, I gain nothing from adding a comment to your image. You are the one who should benefit.<br/> <br/>Good luck in future challenges.</td>', 'So despite another commentor saying essentially the same thing as me it''s me who is at fault for not seeing the challenge? Thanks for the PM and I quote.. ooooh, I''m sorry.  I realise now I should have done a butterfly sitting on gnome.  Live and learn. IMHO to become a better photographer you need to accept criticism better, it''s not personal, I don''t know you, I gain nothing from adding a comment to your image. You are the one who should benefit. Good luck in future challenges.', '2003-08-06 04:04:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(378154, 31144, 3290, '<td valign="top">Congrats, Bob. Great shot - well done.</td>', 'Congrats, Bob. Great shot - well done.', '2003-08-06 04:21:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(378158, 31144, 8522, '<td valign="top">Wow, thanks everyone... an unexpected result! There were so many great shots in this challenge, and I''m much more fond of many of my other entries that didn''t do so well!<br/>And I know now what a damselfly is!</td>', 'Wow, thanks everyone... an unexpected result! There were so many great shots in this challenge, and I''m much more fond of many of my other entries that didn''t do so well!And I know now what a damselfly is!', '2003-08-06 04:23:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(378163, 31144, 8860, '<td valign="top">Well done Bob - top job. Beautiful capture.</td>', 'Well done Bob - top job. Beautiful capture.', '2003-08-06 04:29:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(378170, 30677, 10635, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by vtruan:</b></div><hr/><i>Oh sweet-pea... to bad the bee shows motion.  Otherwise nice capture.</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>There was a clearer one, but the bee was in a worse position, so I thought I would try it, as it was my first challenge.</td>', 'Originally posted by vtruan:Oh sweet-pea... to bad the bee shows motion.  Otherwise nice capture.  There was a clearer one, but the bee was in a worse position, so I thought I would try it, as it was my first challenge.', '2003-08-06 04:42:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(378172, 30677, 10635, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by carlosgustavo:</b></div><hr/><i>no flowers. ring any bell?</i></td></tr></table> <br/>It said the flower must NOT be the main subject.  The main subject here is the bee, although maybe the flower overpowers it.</td>', 'Originally posted by carlosgustavo:no flowers. ring any bell? It said the flower must NOT be the main subject.  The main subject here is the bee, although maybe the flower overpowers it.', '2003-08-06 04:44:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(378174, 31012, 8860, '<td valign="top">I gave this a 10, but never left a comment. I think this is a winner. You''ve captured a lovely moment beautifully, even flawlessly. A well deserved placing.</td>', 'I gave this a 10, but never left a comment. I think this is a winner. You''ve captured a lovely moment beautifully, even flawlessly. A well deserved placing.', '2003-08-06 04:45:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(378176, 30677, 10635, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by rickhd13:</b></div><hr/><i>nice macro attempt, details in the bee are a little off</i></td></tr></table> <br/>Thanks!  Its typical, the challenge date closes and I take a better photo of a bee and separately a butterfly on a flower.</td>', 'Originally posted by rickhd13:nice macro attempt, details in the bee are a little off Thanks!  Its typical, the challenge date closes and I take a better photo of a bee and separately a butterfly on a flower.', '2003-08-06 04:47:12.000000', NULL, 0),
