(379312, 31144, 748, '<td valign="top">Congrats on a really nice shot.  I just saw one of these rascals the other day, but couldn''t get him to cooperate.  From an old Essex boy, what a smashing shot!</td>', 'Congrats on a really nice shot.  I just saw one of these rascals the other day, but couldn''t get him to cooperate.  From an old Essex boy, what a smashing shot!', '2003-08-06 20:08:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(379314, 31168, 2221, '<td valign="top">Hey, jetzt hab ich dich! Bring my garden dwarf back!!!<br/>Just kidding ;-) But when I saw this photo during the challenge I immedeatly remembered a story I read in the newspaper about how somebodys garden dwarf went on vacation and sent a postcard back with a picture of himself at a caribbean beach. Your dwarf seem to have been catched by the same kind of wanderlust. :-) I like the humour in the photo and I think it''s also technically a great photo. So I gave you a 10, but I didn''t finish voting on the 20% so that probably didn''t help you much.<br/>Anyway, I would also love to see the complete album at the end or maybe the dwarf will now have an appearance on DPC more often?<br/></td>', 'Hey, jetzt hab ich dich! Bring my garden dwarf back!!!Just kidding ;-) But when I saw this photo during the challenge I immedeatly remembered a story I read in the newspaper about how somebodys garden dwarf went on vacation and sent a postcard back with a picture of himself at a caribbean beach. Your dwarf seem to have been catched by the same kind of wanderlust. :-) I like the humour in the photo and I think it''s also technically a great photo. So I gave you a 10, but I didn''t finish voting on the 20% so that probably didn''t help you much.Anyway, I would also love to see the complete album at the end or maybe the dwarf will now have an appearance on DPC more often?', '2003-08-06 20:09:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(379318, 31012, 748, '<td valign="top">My thanks to all for your votes and kind words.  I really feel honored to share the front page with the other winners.  For BabyHeads, this was real and not staged, and the subjects co-operated quite well.  They minded their business and I tried not to interfere.  I picked this one out of about 40 shots.  It helped to have a sunflower as tall as myself so I could stand up and set up the tripod and wait for the right moments.  At one point there were 4 bees on the same flower head!</td>', 'My thanks to all for your votes and kind words.  I really feel honored to share the front page with the other winners.  For BabyHeads, this was real and not staged, and the subjects co-operated quite well.  They minded their business and I tried not to interfere.  I picked this one out of about 40 shots.  It helped to have a sunflower as tall as myself so I could stand up and set up the tripod and wait for the right moments.  At one point there were 4 bees on the same flower head!', '2003-08-06 20:17:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(379409, 30233, 6359, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by magnetic9999:</b></div><hr/><i>i thought this was awesome. if i had commented i would have suggested redoing it the same but setting up cam on a tripod with timer so that you''re not taking the pic in the pic itself... :)</i></td></tr></table> <br/>Just like magnetic9999 said, However I would have not thought of but would have like to have the camera on the ground with selftimer and the butterfly would be blocking the reflection. This would have been a great shot.  It still could be a great shot, if you re-take it.<br/> <br/>Forgot to mention. not sure if you wnated the angle to be cutoff.<br/>lastly you may want to have a wider shot so that you can straighten the bottom edge. currently, pedestal is not level with the bottom of the frame.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-08-06 21:08:05.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by magnetic9999:i thought this was awesome. if i had commented i would have suggested redoing it the same but setting up cam on a tripod with timer so that you''re not taking the pic in the pic itself... :) Just like magnetic9999 said, However I would have not thought of but would have like to have the camera on the ground with selftimer and the butterfly would be blocking the reflection. This would have been a great shot.  It still could be a great shot, if you re-take it. Forgot to mention. not sure if you wnated the angle to be cutoff.lastly you may want to have a wider shot so that you can straighten the bottom edge. currently, pedestal is not level with the bottom of the frame.', '2003-08-06 22:03:05.000000', '2003-08-06 22:08:05.000000', 0),
(379428, 30736, 7743, '<td valign="top">I want to thank everyone for their comments.  I agree that the focus is a little soft.  This is probably due to the use of the diopters.  Without them though I wouldn''t have been able to get close enough.  As it was, I had to crop this image out of a larger image.<br/> <br/>asitv, the lighting is just the evening sun, nothing special.  The focus point was set right on the bug.</td>', 'I want to thank everyone for their comments.  I agree that the focus is a little soft.  This is probably due to the use of the diopters.  Without them though I wouldn''t have been able to get close enough.  As it was, I had to crop this image out of a larger image. asitv, the lighting is just the evening sun, nothing special.  The focus point was set right on the bug.', '2003-08-06 22:18:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(379472, 30171, 9436, '<td valign="top">This is THE best shot of the challenge. To all the nay-sayers - of course it is a toy ant! You should have titled it, "Now where did I leave my toy ant?" GREAT SHOT!</td>', 'This is THE best shot of the challenge. To all the nay-sayers - of course it is a toy ant! You should have titled it, "Now where did I leave my toy ant?" GREAT SHOT!', '2003-08-06 23:25:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(379832, 30869, 9854, '<td valign="top">Sorry, this is a bit late. Anyhow....<br/> <br/>Framing is good. Subject is a bit lacking, though. I would have preferred seeing more of interesting objects in the frame than just plants. Perhaps have someone actually BE there. BTW, is this Fort Ilocandia? I was there once and I absolutely loved the place. The beach however, was more for contemplation, rather than the normal kind of beach fun. It was very surfy and desolate (would really be a good subject for the challenge!) when I was there in October years ago (I think 1995). Seems like it''s time for me for a second visit!</td>', 'Sorry, this is a bit late. Anyhow.... Framing is good. Subject is a bit lacking, though. I would have preferred seeing more of interesting objects in the frame than just plants. Perhaps have someone actually BE there. BTW, is this Fort Ilocandia? I was there once and I absolutely loved the place. The beach however, was more for contemplation, rather than the normal kind of beach fun. It was very surfy and desolate (would really be a good subject for the challenge!) when I was there in October years ago (I think 1995). Seems like it''s time for me for a second visit!', '2003-08-07 03:37:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(379849, 30286, 7531, '<td valign="top">I haven''t looked at the In the Garden Challenge, but I have seen the three winners, what can I say! This photo portrays the subject beautifully, the colours are gentle and soft, just like a graden should be. It reminds me so much of an afternoon in the garden of my old house in England especially now that I am living in Turkey. Well done</td>', 'I haven''t looked at the In the Garden Challenge, but I have seen the three winners, what can I say! This photo portrays the subject beautifully, the colours are gentle and soft, just like a graden should be. It reminds me so much of an afternoon in the garden of my old house in England especially now that I am living in Turkey. Well done', '2003-08-07 04:06:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(380453, 30999, 4266, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by hgpayne:</b></div><hr/><i>The main subject here seems to be dead flowers, which violates the challenge... but wait... I do see a bug -- perhaps this is the subject. If so, we need to be closer to really see him.</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I agree with everybody''s comments.  The thing is, I really want to participate at DPChallenge, so I am trying right now just to make each week''s contest.  Also, I know my skills are limited, so I am looking forward to any help or comments I might get.</td>', 'Originally posted by hgpayne:The main subject here seems to be dead flowers, which violates the challenge... but wait... I do see a bug -- perhaps this is the subject. If so, we need to be closer to really see him.  I agree with everybody''s comments.  The thing is, I really want to participate at DPChallenge, so I am trying right now just to make each week''s contest.  Also, I know my skills are limited, so I am looking forward to any help or comments I might get.', '2003-08-07 11:48:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(380903, 30171, 4008, '<td valign="top">Thanks Meggie and Eric (and others during the challenge) glad you like my shot, I still like it a lot myself. And I keep wondering, how on earth could I have used a real bug ? I don''t kill animals for pictures. And with myself in the picture using the self timer it needed to sit still for 10 seconds....<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-08-07 15:48:39.</i></td>', 'Thanks Meggie and Eric (and others during the challenge) glad you like my shot, I still like it a lot myself. And I keep wondering, how on earth could I have used a real bug ? I don''t kill animals for pictures. And with myself in the picture using the self timer it needed to sit still for 10 seconds....', '2003-08-07 16:18:19.000000', '2003-08-07 16:48:39.000000', 0),
