(385521, 31011, 133, '<td valign="top">Thanks to everyone for your positive comments.  I don''t know why the out of focus head bothers so many people.  Actually my thought at the time was the composition placement of the angle for the wings, not the focus.  As to the glares, I feel they help to give the appearance of the membrane part of the wings.  Thanks again.<br/> <br/><a href="//web.tampabay.rr.com/swilli41/www" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Suzanne Williams Photography</a></td>', 'Thanks to everyone for your positive comments.  I don''t know why the out of focus head bothers so many people.  Actually my thought at the time was the composition placement of the angle for the wings, not the focus.  As to the glares, I feel they help to give the appearance of the membrane part of the wings.  Thanks again. Suzanne Williams Photography', '2003-08-12 19:01:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(385600, 31001, 2752, '<td valign="top">I can''t imagine how anyone could vote 1''s-3''s.  this is a beautiful contrast of mist and green,a good composition and the people on the path really show the tallness of the trees. This was a 10 from me and I would have given you a 10 without the people.</td>', 'I can''t imagine how anyone could vote 1''s-3''s.  this is a beautiful contrast of mist and green,a good composition and the people on the path really show the tallness of the trees. This was a 10 from me and I would have given you a 10 without the people.', '2003-08-12 20:37:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(385740, 30303, 6202, '<td valign="top"><br/>*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>This is a fantastic image the color is good the dof used works well the focus is good, there really isn''t a thing I would change on this photo. <br/> <br/>Your composition is exceptionally well done, I think what hurt you is it is a little week for in the garden.  The photo could have been anywhere there was grass or a pine tree and that probably is the one thing that hurt you.  <br/> <br/>Overall this is a wonderful shot...keep up the good work.</td>', '*Critique Club* This is a fantastic image the color is good the dof used works well the focus is good, there really isn''t a thing I would change on this photo.  Your composition is exceptionally well done, I think what hurt you is it is a little week for in the garden.  The photo could have been anywhere there was grass or a pine tree and that probably is the one thing that hurt you.   Overall this is a wonderful shot...keep up the good work.', '2003-08-13 00:03:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(385746, 30583, 6202, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>This was a well thought out idea but it appears to have been rushed when you took the photo.  The melon is not in real good focus it tends to be softer to the right side as does the right hand as well. <br/> <br/>Your composition isn''t bad, if you didn''t use an unsharpening mask in the future try it and see if that helps/</td>', '*Critique Club* This was a well thought out idea but it appears to have been rushed when you took the photo.  The melon is not in real good focus it tends to be softer to the right side as does the right hand as well.  Your composition isn''t bad, if you didn''t use an unsharpening mask in the future try it and see if that helps/', '2003-08-13 00:05:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(385748, 31051, 811, '<td valign="top">CRITIQUE CLUB CRITIQUE<br/>by karmat<br/> <br/>I did not vote in this challenge, because of time issues, but I think you have done an excellent and creative job of meeting the challenge.  I guess my only beef would be that it wasn''t really "in" the garden, but other than that, I think it is an awesome idea. <br/> <br/>I do think the reflection detracts a little.  At first it didn''t bother me, but as i looked at it, my eyes began to cross and it was like part of the picture was out of focus (not the deliberately out of focus part,).  I like that the plant is so well lit and visible in front of the blurry greenery outside.  It would have been neat to have a cityscape behind it, but I guess we can''t have everything.<br/> <br/>Something about the shadowed part across the bottom makes it feel unbalanced to me.  Perhaps if it were cropped so that just the shelf, and not the shadow were showing this could be helped OR give just a bit more room on the right.<br/> <br/>Good work and best wishes to you in future challenges.<br/> <br/>karma</td>', 'CRITIQUE CLUB CRITIQUEby karmat I did not vote in this challenge, because of time issues, but I think you have done an excellent and creative job of meeting the challenge.  I guess my only beef would be that it wasn''t really "in" the garden, but other than that, I think it is an awesome idea.  I do think the reflection detracts a little.  At first it didn''t bother me, but as i looked at it, my eyes began to cross and it was like part of the picture was out of focus (not the deliberately out of focus part,).  I like that the plant is so well lit and visible in front of the blurry greenery outside.  It would have been neat to have a cityscape behind it, but I guess we can''t have everything. Something about the shadowed part across the bottom makes it feel unbalanced to me.  Perhaps if it were cropped so that just the shelf, and not the shadow were showing this could be helped OR give just a bit more room on the right. Good work and best wishes to you in future challenges. karma', '2003-08-13 00:06:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(385770, 31240, 2952, '<td valign="top">This happened to be one of many pictures I just had around that I thought would fit the theme, but I guess my effect wasn''t clear in my explanation.  A soft focus filter was on the lens of my camera -- i.e., people saying it''s "blurry" are in fact right --- it''s meant to be.  If it weren''t, the picture would be worthless (which it pretty much is already; I know.).<br/> <br/>Hey, but at least I got your attention.  Better things are to come.  Guess I should have put in a "leaf" or "insect" shot; being somewhat creative with trash shot got me nowhere.  :-)</td>', 'This happened to be one of many pictures I just had around that I thought would fit the theme, but I guess my effect wasn''t clear in my explanation.  A soft focus filter was on the lens of my camera -- i.e., people saying it''s "blurry" are in fact right --- it''s meant to be.  If it weren''t, the picture would be worthless (which it pretty much is already; I know.). Hey, but at least I got your attention.  Better things are to come.  Guess I should have put in a "leaf" or "insect" shot; being somewhat creative with trash shot got me nowhere.  :-)', '2003-08-13 00:34:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(385772, 30869, 811, '<td valign="top">CRITIQUE CLUB CRITIQUE<br/>by karmat<br/> <br/>Very interesting take on the challenge.  It is a ''garden'' without being blatant about it.  I really like the rich colors evident here, and it seems that you have done well at capturing the beauty of the place.  My only gripe with the picture is the exposure.  The lit part is almost blown out, yet the shadows complete hide any potential detail.  I, for one, am not that good at adjusting or compensating for exposure (still learning this aspect), but jmsetzler and gordon are both very good at it.  I am sure if you contacted them, they could give you some pointers on it, if you wanted it. <br/> <br/>Compositionally, I like how the light on the floor attracts your attention and leads you out the gate.  It is an interesting picture that really makes the viewer want to see more of this place, or learn about it.  <br/> <br/>Good work and best to you in future challenges.<br/> <br/>karmat</td>', 'CRITIQUE CLUB CRITIQUEby karmat Very interesting take on the challenge.  It is a ''garden'' without being blatant about it.  I really like the rich colors evident here, and it seems that you have done well at capturing the beauty of the place.  My only gripe with the picture is the exposure.  The lit part is almost blown out, yet the shadows complete hide any potential detail.  I, for one, am not that good at adjusting or compensating for exposure (still learning this aspect), but jmsetzler and gordon are both very good at it.  I am sure if you contacted them, they could give you some pointers on it, if you wanted it.  Compositionally, I like how the light on the floor attracts your attention and leads you out the gate.  It is an interesting picture that really makes the viewer want to see more of this place, or learn about it.   Good work and best to you in future challenges. karmat', '2003-08-13 00:37:04.000000', NULL, 0),
